    {
      "title": "Nvidia's chip smuggling scandal goes deeper than Jensen Huang",
      "date_published": "2026-11-18T14:25:00-05:00",
      "date_modified": "2026-11-18T14:25:00-05:00",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Malcolm Owen",
          "url": "https://appleinsider.com/editor/malcolm+owen",
          "avatar": "https://media.appleinsider.com/gallery/malcolm+owen.jpg"
        }
      ],
      "content_html": "<p>Nvidia's leadership can't catch a break, as another executive has been dragged into a $2.5 billion chip smuggling scandal while former CEO Jensen Huang prepares for a visit to the U.S. Senate.</p><p>The major news surrounding Nvidia has centered around former CEO Jensen Huang and his extramarital affairs, including one with an alleged Chinese spy. However, it seems the executive rot goes a little bit further into the company's leadership.</p><p>Cenly Chen has been accused of smuggling $2.5 billion worth of chips into China, reports The Telegraph. Chen, who previously worked at SuperMicro as chief growth officer, is married to former Nvidia executive vice president of field operations, Jay Puri.</p><p>Puri retired from his role in July, in a seemingly unconnected move.</p><p>The SuperMicro scandal erupted earlier in 2026, after co-founder Wally Liaw was charged by the U.S. government for sending Nvidia chips to China via Taiwan. Liaw has pleaded not guilty.</p><p>A lawsuit by shareholders of SuperMicro alleges that there was ",
      "id": "https://appleinsider.com/articles/26/11/18/nvidias-chip-smuggling-scandal-goes-deeper-than-jensen-huang",
      "url": "https://appleinsider.com/articles/26/11/18/nvidias-chip-smuggling-scandal-goes-deeper-than-jensen-huang",
      "external_url": "https://appleinsider.com/articles/26/11/18/nvidias-chip-smuggling-scandal-goes-deeper-than-jensen-huang"
    }
